      "difficulty": 3,
      "passage": "In colonial America, owning a printing press was as much a political act as a commercial one. **Because type, paper, and ink were costly and difficult to import, most early printers survived only by also serving as postmasters, booksellers, or government contractors.** Benjamin Franklin, for instance, leveraged a public printing contract to subsidize his more daring pamphlets.",
