      "difficulty": 3,
      "passage": "It is tempting to think a longer bridge simply needs thicker cables. **In reality, beyond a certain span the cables grow so heavy that they must support not only the deck but also their own enormous weight, a problem that quickly outpaces any gain from added thickness.** This is why the longest suspension bridges push materials to their physical limits.",
