      "passage": "A jazz ensemble can sound chaotic to the untrained ear, yet its players are following an unspoken framework. They share an agreed harmonic structure, a steady underlying pulse, and a customary order in which soloists take turns. **Within these constraints, each musician is free to invent, knowing that the shared rules will keep even daring departures from descending into noise.** Far from limiting creativity, the framework is what makes group improvisation possible.",
