      "skill": "text-structure",
      "domain": "Craft and Structure",
      "difficulty": 5,
      "passage": "Critics of public libraries argue that taxpayers should not subsidize services that the market could provide. Defenders respond that libraries deliver benefits markets routinely overlook. **A child who develops a reading habit in a free library may, decades later, become a more productive worker and citizen—a gain too diffuse and delayed for any private bookstore to capture or charge for.** Such spillover effects, economists note, are precisely what justify public provision.",
