      "skill": "text-structure",
      "domain": "Craft and Structure",
      "difficulty": 5,
      "passage": "Many plants rely on ants to carry their seeds, rewarding the insects with a fatty appendage called an elaiosome that is rich in nutrients. **One might expect the ants, having eaten this prize, to discard the seed somewhere harmful, yet they typically deposit it in nutrient-rich refuse piles that make ideal seedbeds.** This arrangement, in which the discarded seed germinates in a fertile microhabitat, helps explain why ant-dispersed plants are so widespread in nutrient-poor soils.",
