      "difficulty": 4,
      "passage": "During the Bronze Age, the alloy that gave the era its name required tin, a metal found in only a few scattered deposits across Eurasia. **Because tin and copper rarely occurred near each other, communities had to move one or both metals over considerable distances to combine them.** Archaeologists trace these movements through chemical fingerprints in surviving artifacts, reconstructing trade routes that spanned thousands of kilometers.",
