      "difficulty": 5,
      "passage": "Coastal engineers have long built concrete seawalls to blunt the force of storm surges, but such barriers are costly and can fail catastrophically. **Mangrove forests, by contrast, dissipate wave energy gradually through their dense tangle of roots and even rebuild themselves by trapping sediment as they grow.** Several storm-prone nations have begun planting mangroves alongside or in place of hardened defenses.",
