      "domain": "Craft and Structure",
      "difficulty": 4,
      "passage": "When a baker kneads dough, the proteins in flour link together into an elastic network called gluten that can trap gas. **This network is what allows dough to swell rather than collapse, holding the bubbles of carbon dioxide that yeast produces during fermentation.** Without sufficient gluten, even vigorously fermented dough yields a dense, flat loaf.",
