      "skill": "text-structure",
      "domain": "Craft and Structure",
      "difficulty": 5,
      "passage": "Bees and butterflies struggle to survive in cities, where flowering plants are sparse and separated by stretches of pavement. **Some urban planners argue that scattering small patches of native blooms across rooftops and medians would do little good unless those patches are close enough for insects to travel between them.** Designing such a connected network, rather than a few isolated gardens, is now a central goal of pollinator-friendly city planning.",
