      "skill": "text-structure",
      "domain": "Craft and Structure",
      "difficulty": 4,
      "passage": "Animals that live in scorching deserts often avoid the midday heat by staying active only after dark. **Yet darkness brings its own hazard, since the same cool air that spares an animal from overheating can drop temperatures low enough to sap a small body's energy.** To cope, many nocturnal desert dwellers shelter in burrows whose walls buffer them against both extremes.",
