      "skill": "text-structure",
      "domain": "Craft and Structure",
      "difficulty": 5,
      "passage": "When the first printed atlases appeared in the late fifteenth century, publishers faced a problem unknown to scribes copying maps by hand: every printed copy was identical, so an error engraved into a plate spread to thousands of books. **This rigidity, however, eventually became an advantage, for once a map was carefully corrected, the correction too could be reproduced flawlessly across an entire edition.** Cartographers thus learned to invest heavily in verifying a single master plate.",
