      "skill": "text-structure",
      "domain": "Craft and Structure",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "passage": "City-dwelling foxes behave quite differently from their rural relatives, who tend to avoid open ground and unfamiliar objects. **Urban foxes, by comparison, grow bolder over generations, learning to cross busy streets, raid bins, and rest in plain sight of people.** Researchers suspect that the constant presence of humans gradually filters out the most fearful individuals.",
