      "domain": "Craft and Structure",
      "difficulty": 4,
      "passage": "A bat hunting in cluttered surroundings faces a problem: if it called too loudly, the flood of overlapping echoes from leaves and branches would drown out the faint echo of its prey. **To avoid this, many species lower their call volume as they close in on a target, sharpening their focus on the returning echo that matters most.** This fine adjustment lets a bat track a single moth even amid a tangle of vegetation.",
