      "passage": "Giant kelp can grow nearly two feet in a single day, forming underwater forests that shelter fish, snails, and sea otters alike. **When sea urchin populations explode, however, the grazers can mow down a flourishing forest faster than it regenerates, leaving behind a barren expanse of rock.** Otters, by preying on the urchins, often hold this destructive pressure in check.",
