      "difficulty": 3,
      "passage": "The abacus stores numbers as the positions of beads on rods, with each rod representing a place value. **A skilled user shifts beads in patterns so practiced that the hands seem to move before the mind has consciously decided what to do.** This blend of physical memory and positional notation let merchants tally large sums faster than many could with pen and paper.",
