      "domain": "Craft and Structure",
      "difficulty": 5,
      "passage": "Permafrost has long been treated as a stable storehouse, locking away ancient plant carbon in frozen ground. **Yet as the ground thaws, microbes resume breaking down that organic matter, releasing carbon dioxide and methane that further warm the climate.** Modelers warn that this feedback could accelerate warming beyond what most projections currently assume, though the pace remains uncertain.",
