      "skill": "text-structure",
      "domain": "Craft and Structure",
      "difficulty": 4,
      "passage": "Early folk-song collectors traveled the countryside with notebooks, transcribing melodies by ear from singers they met. **Because a transcriber could capture only what one hearing allowed, the printed versions often smoothed away the slides, drones, and rhythmic looseness that gave the songs their character.** Later collectors who carried recording machines preserved these textures, and scholars now treat such recordings as far closer to the living tradition.",
