      "difficulty": 5,
      "passage": "A deep river canyon can look like the work of a single catastrophic flood, its walls cut as if by one violent stroke. **In most cases, however, the gorge records millions of years of patient erosion, as a river removed grain after grain while the land beneath it slowly rose.** The exposed rock layers, read from rim to river, thus form a calendar that geologists use to date events long predating any human witness.",
