      "skill": "text-structure",
      "domain": "Craft and Structure",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "passage": "A refracting telescope gathers light through a large lens and bends it to a focus, where a smaller eyepiece magnifies the image. **One drawback of such lenses is that they bend different colors of light by slightly different amounts, fringing bright objects with false color.** To avoid this problem, many large modern telescopes use curved mirrors instead, since a mirror reflects all colors to the same focus.",
