      "skill": "text-structure",
      "domain": "Craft and Structure",
      "difficulty": 4,
      "passage": "Beneath a forest floor, fungal threads weave among tree roots, exchanging nutrients for the sugars the trees produce. **Recent experiments using labeled carbon show that these threads can also shuttle resources from one tree to another, sometimes from a sunlit tree to a shaded seedling.** Some ecologists describe the resulting web as a shared economy, though others caution that the trees may simply be losing carbon the fungi happen to redistribute.",
