      "difficulty": 4,
      "passage": "In many medieval towns, a craft guild controlled who could practice a given trade, setting prices, standards, and the length of apprenticeships. **Supporters of the guilds noted that these rules protected buyers from shoddy goods and guaranteed members a stable living.** Critics, then and now, reply that the same rules choked off competition and kept newcomers and outsiders from entering the trade at all.",
