      "passage": "Early machine-translation systems worked by replacing each word in a sentence with its dictionary equivalent in another language. **The results were often comically wrong, because a single word can carry several meanings that only context can settle.** Later systems improved by analyzing whole phrases and, more recently, by training on millions of human-translated sentences. Even now, though, idioms and cultural references continue to trip up the most advanced programs.",
