      "difficulty": 5,
      "passage": "Radio astronomers study the universe by collecting faint radio waves that ordinary optical telescopes cannot detect. **Because a single dish would have to be impossibly large to see fine detail, astronomers instead link many smaller dishes spread across great distances and combine their signals.** This technique, called interferometry, lets a network of antennas act as one instrument with the resolving power of a dish hundreds of miles wide.",
